[[Try again->AQ8]]

:: AImg {"position":"1500,1650","size":"150,100"}
|m>[Right! The instruments were designed to stay on the Moon and send information to Earth for years, without anyone having to bring them back.]
|m>[💡 Fact: We kept sending data for about 6 years, until NASA shut down the experiment network in 1977.]
|q>[Imagination question: If you could choose the name of the Moon car you'd use to explore the lunar surface, what would you call it?]

[[I've got my answer! ✨->AEnd]]

:: AEnd {"position":"1500,1800","size":"150,100"}
|big>[🏅]
|m>[I hope you enjoyed the trip! As a reward for playing along, I'll share a couple of little secrets that very few people know. Keep them safe! 🤫]
|m>[🤫 Secret 1: The First Moon Car!]
|m>[Did you know? Apollo 15 was the first mission to use a Lunar Roving Vehicle on the Moon! It was an electric vehicle powered by batteries.]
|m>[🤫 Secret 2: A Long Stay on the Moon!]
|m>[Did you know? Apollo 15 astronauts stayed on the lunar surface for about 66 hours and 55 minutes, making it a much longer exploration than earlier Apollo landing missions.]
